Since 76cf0d750 (GH #1436) the R2007+ entity material flags come before the
plot style flags, so an explicit material is LibreDWG's `material` handle in
both directions. Without DEBUG_CLASSES the encoder still sets every
material_flags 3 to 0 ("Disabling MATERIAL handle"), because MATERIALs from
DXF imports are replaced by placeholders (encode.c). The MATERIALs of a
drawing built with the add API are kept (add-mesh-material patch), so their
entity handles are kept too.

diff --git a/src/common_entity_data.spec b/src/common_entity_data.spec
index 10dd702..e24efc7 100644
--- a/src/common_entity_data.spec
+++ b/src/common_entity_data.spec
@@ -517,7 +517,10 @@
     {
 #ifndef DEBUG_CLASSES
 #ifdef IS_ENCODER
-      if (FIELD_VALUE (material_flags) == 3)
+      // MATERIALs made by the add API are complete, so their handles are
+      // kept (encode.c keeps the objects, see DWG_OPTS_ADDAPI)
+      if (FIELD_VALUE (material_flags) == 3
+          && !(dwg->opts & DWG_OPTS_ADDAPI))
         {
           LOG_WARN ("Disabling MATERIAL handle\n");
             FIELD_VALUE (material_flags) = 0;
